# tarball, and the same manifest always produces a byte-identical tarball. Its
# sha256 is in aosp/aosp-source.sha256. patches/<dir>.patch is applied on top at
# build time; it is not in the tarball.
#
# Changing any non-comment line changes the tarball's name and sha256: run
# ./aosp-source.sh generate --update and commit both files together.
#
# Format:
#   tag <aosp release tag>                       - the release the commits belong to
#   <dir> <repository> <commit> [<path>...]      - one repository; with paths, only
#                                                  those paths are exported

